# ---------- Expo / React Native ----------
.expo/
.expo-shared/
dist/
web-build/
*.jsbundle
*.orig.*

# Native projects are generated by `expo prebuild`; native config lives in app.config.ts.
# NOTE: apps/mobile/modules/** (local Expo native modules) is deliberately NOT ignored.
/apps/mobile/ios/
/apps/mobile/android/

# Signing material — never commit
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
*.keystore
*.jks

# ...with one deliberate exception. This is a DEBUG keystore whose password is the
# well-known 'android'. It is committed so the Android SHA-1 stays identical across machines
# and CI — Google OAuth registers a specific (package, fingerprint) pair, so a per-machine
# keystore would mean sign-in only worked on one laptop. It cannot sign a release: the upload
# key is generated and held by EAS and never lives here.
!apps/mobile/credentials/debug.keystore

# ---------- Secrets / service config ----------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist
# ...except the Android one, which is NOT a secret and has to be committed.
#
# It holds a project id, a project number, the package name and an Android API key — every one
# of which is already extractable from any installed APK, because this file is compiled into the
# binary. Firebase's own guidance is that it is safe to check in.
#
# It has to be, in fact: EAS uploads the git repo, so a gitignored config is simply absent from
# the build, and Android push then fails at runtime with nothing to point at.
#
# Verified before committing that ours carries **zero `oauth_client` entries** — the Android app
# was registered in Firebase with no SHA-1 on purpose. That matters: a SHA-1 there would mint a
# competing OAuth client for `com.chukta.app` in the Firebase project (522412396487), while
# Google sign-in is registered in a different project (153443409774), and two owners for one
# package is the usual cause of DEVELOPER_ERROR. If a SHA-1 is ever added in Firebase, re-check
# this file before trusting sign-in.
!apps/mobile/google-services.json
supabase/.env
supabase/.branches/
supabase/.temp/
.supabase/

# ---------- Build / test output ----------
coverage/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
maestro/**/screenshots/
maestro/**/*.mp4

# NOTE: design-reference/screens/support.js and design-reference/assets/image-slot.js are
# vendored third-party prototype-viewer runtime, deliberately tracked so the reference
# screens still render in a browser. See design-reference/README.md.

# Gradle output from local Expo modules. Was tracked (778 files, including .aar and .dex),
# and with requireCommit these uploaded to every EAS build.
apps/mobile/modules/*/android/build/

# Throwaway design prototypes for approval. The keepers live in design-reference/.
prototypes/
